From 37d4782303d3f208b6345a19cdf82d9b03d89dd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:48:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0128: manual HUD settings are a delta from the auto edge
 anchor; compass takes an extra +128

V1.3.17 (log-33) showed the manual settings landing one whole edge away
from where the player dragged them: the editor shows the element at its
edge-anchored default and records the drag from there, but the game applied
the manual offset as an absolute offset from the game's default layout,
replacing the edge -- coins manual 16,-3 landed at default+16 instead of
edge+16, and the moons manual 293,169 likewise. The manual offset is now
ADDED to the edge anchor, so dragging in the editor moves the element by
the same amount in the game, and a manual element still follows the aspect
(as the editor does). An old saved setting (recorded as a drag from the
edge) is now read correctly with no migration.

The compass dial is centred in its 340-wide 'PicStrap' strip, so the plain
edge puts the strip at the screen edge but the dial ~128 short of it (the
V1.3.17 screenshot puts the dial's right edge ~155 layout points from the
screen edge while the lives heart is at the edge). The compass takes an
extra +128 on its edge anchor (auto and manual base), bringing the dial --
and the hints text in the strip -- to the edge, matching the editor, which
centres the compass on the lives column. The strip's right edge then sits
~100 past the screen edge; the strip is transparent there.

Not fixed here: the moon dots are not Counter children (log-20 lists no dot
panes under the Counter, and none anywhere), so if the real dots are not
Counter children the manual move will not carry them -- a probe is needed
to identify the dots' pane/parent. The hints pane name TxtGuide01 is the
wrong pane for the visible '+ menu / - map' text (log-20 puts it at global
(798,86), centre-screen, while the visible hints are at ~1340) -- a probe
is needed to identify the real hints pane name. No state-page layout
change; BINDING v6 -> v7; HUD_EDGE_WORDS regenerated (744 words).
---
 dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_edge.c | 85 ++++++++++++++++++-------
 dm/games/0100000000010000/patches.py | 94 ++++++++++++++--------------
 2 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 70 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_edge.c b/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_edge.c
index 62a84aa..7375646 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_edge.c
+++ b/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_edge.c
@@ -8,10 +8,17 @@
 // (coins, regional coins, moons) move left on a wider screen and right on a narrower one; the
 // right widgets (compass, lives, hints) move right on a wider screen and left
 // on a narrower one. A manual setting made in the launcher's HUD editor (0119)
-// overrides the automatic edge anchor for that element: it is moved, resized
-// and hidden exactly as the player set it, and it stays put when the screen
-// aspect changes, while elements with no manual setting keep following the
-// aspect. A hidden element is moved off-screen, so it is not drawn.
+// is a delta from that automatic edge anchor (0128): the editor shows the
+// element at its edge-anchored default and the player drags from there, so the
+// manual offset is added to the edge -- dragging in the editor moves the
+// element by the same amount in the game -- while elements with no manual
+// setting keep following the aspect. A hidden element is moved off-screen, so
+// it is not drawn. The compass takes one extra offset (0128): its pane
+// 'PicStrap' is a 340-wide strip and the visible dial is centred in it, so
+// the plain edge puts the strip at the screen edge but the dial ~128 short
+// of it; the extra offset brings the dial (and the hints text in the strip)
+// to the edge, matching the editor, which centres the compass on the lives
+// column.
 //
 // The automatic offset comes from the screen aspect the host already writes
 // into the frame-step state page (loader.c dm_fps_state_apply, state +0x58:
@@ -31,12 +38,14 @@
 // DM_HUD_COMPASS / DM_HUD_LIFE / DM_HUD_COINS / DM_HUD_MOONS / DM_HUD_HINTS
 // environment variables from the player's editor choices before the game starts):
 //   +0x200: 15 floats, per element (dx, dy, k): compass, lives, coins,
-//     moons, hints. dx / dy are layout points (the 1280x720 space), absolute
-//     from the game's own layout position -- NOT added to the automatic edge
-//     offset, so a manual element stays put when the aspect changes. A drag
-//     down the screen is a negative dy (the layout is y-up); the launcher
-//     negates its y-down drag when it writes the value. k is the element's
-//     size, 0.6 to 1.8 (the editor's slider), 1 is the game's own size.
+//     moons, hints. dx / dy are layout points (the 1280x720 space), a DELTA
+//     from the automatic edge anchor (0128): the launcher's editor shows the
+//     element at its edge-anchored default and records the drag from there,
+//     so the manual offset is ADDED to the edge -- dragging in the editor
+//     moves the element by the same amount in the game. A drag down the
+//     screen is a negative dy (the layout is y-up); the launcher negates its
+//     y-down drag when it writes the value. k is the element's size, 0.6 to
+//     1.8 (the editor's slider), 1 is the game's own size.
 //   +0x240: u32 manual mask (bit i: element i has a manual setting).
 //   +0x244: u32 hidden mask (bit i: element i is hidden).
 // The state page starts zeroed, so an unwritten block reads as no manual
@@ -67,6 +76,18 @@
 // or an aspect change re-applies instead of being ignored, and a manual
 // element is not re-derived from the automatic offset.
 //
+// (0128) A manual setting is a delta from the automatic edge anchor, NOT an
+// absolute offset from the game's default layout. The old (0119-0127) code
+// treated it as absolute, replacing the edge -- but the editor shows the
+// element at its edge-anchored default and records the drag from there, so
+// a manual element landed one whole edge (140 on iPhone) away from where
+// the player dragged it (V1.3.17, log-33: coins manual 16,-3 landed at
+// default+16 instead of edge+16; the moons manual 293,169 likewise). The
+// manual offset is now ADDED to the edge anchor, so dragging in the editor
+// moves the element by the same amount in the game, and a manual element
+// still follows the aspect (as the editor does). An old saved setting (recorded
+// as a drag from the edge) is now read correctly with no migration.
+//
 // Parent compensation (0123): some matched panes are CHILDREN of other
 // matched panes -- the moon icon (PicIconSh / PicIcon) and its number
 // (TxtTotalShine, when its parent is a Counter) sit inside the moons
@@ -145,6 +166,18 @@ typedef unsigned long uintptr_t;
 // most 1560 wide, so +10000 is safely outside it whatever the aspect.
 #define HUD_HIDE_DX 10000.0f
 
+// The compass dial is centred in its 340-wide 'PicStrap' strip, so the plain
+// edge puts the strip at the screen edge but the dial ~128 short of it (0128:
+// log-20 gives the strip as 340x720; the V1.3.17 screenshot puts the dial's
+// centre ~175 from the strip's left edge, i.e. centred, and the editor
+// centres the compass on the lives column). This extra offset, added to the
+// compass's edge anchor on every aspect, brings the dial (and the hints text
+// in the strip) to the edge. It is a property of the strip's layout (the dial
+// centred in 340), not of the aspect, so it is a constant. The strip's right
+// edge then sits ~100 past the screen edge -- the strip is transparent there,
+// only the dial and the hints text are visible.
+#define HUD_COMPASS_EXTRA 128.0f
+
 // The pane names, as little-endian u32s (no string literal: a literal would
 // sit in .rodata and the code would load its address with an adrp, a
 // relocation, and the embedded words carry no literal pool).
@@ -503,27 +536,33 @@ void hud_edge(void *pane, const float *aspect_ptr, void *table, const float *par
     if (idx < 0) return;   // not a HUD element: leave it alone
 
     // What this element should be, this frame. Priority: hidden first, then
-    // manual, then the automatic edge anchor (0118). A manual setting is an
-    // absolute offset from the game's own layout position -- it replaces the
-    // automatic offset, it is not added to it, so a manual element stays put
-    // when the aspect changes. A hidden element is pushed off-screen; its
-    // manual offset and size do not matter while it is hidden, and it comes
-    // back to its manual (or automatic) place when it is shown again.
+    // manual, then the automatic edge anchor (0118). A manual setting is a
+    // DELTA from the automatic edge anchor (0128): the launcher's editor
+    // shows the element at its edge-anchored default and records the drag
+    // from there, so the manual offset is ADDED to the edge -- dragging in
+    // the editor moves the element by the same amount in the game -- and a
+    // manual element still follows the aspect (as the editor does). The
+    // compass's base anchor also carries the extra offset above (its dial is
+    // centred in the 340-wide strip). A hidden element is pushed off-screen;
+    // its manual offset and size do not matter while it is hidden, and it
+    // comes back to its manual (or automatic) place when it is shown again.
     int manual = (manual_mask >> idx) & 1u;
     int hidden = (hidden_mask >> idx) & 1u;
     float tdx = 0.0f, tdy = 0.0f, tk = 1.0f;
+    float base = (idx == 0 || idx == 1 || idx == 4) ? edge : -edge;
+    if (idx == 0) base += HUD_COMPASS_EXTRA;   // the dial, centred in the 340 strip
     if (!hidden && manual && params) {
-        tdx = hud_edge_clamp_off(params[idx * 3 + 0], 640.0f);
+        tdx = base + hud_edge_clamp_off(params[idx * 3 + 0], 640.0f);
         tdy = hud_edge_clamp_off(params[idx * 3 + 1], 360.0f);
         tk = hud_edge_clamp_k(params[idx * 3 + 2]);
     } else if (!hidden) {
         // Automatic: left widgets (coins, regional coins, moons) take dx = -edge; right
-        // widgets (compass, lives, hints) take dx = +edge. A wider screen
-        // (edge > 0) pushes both outward to the edges; a narrower screen
-        // (edge < 0) pulls both inward so they stay visible and at the
-        // edges. dy is always 0 and the scale is always 1: this patch only
-        // translates, never resizes.
-        tdx = (idx == 0 || idx == 1 || idx == 4) ? edge : -edge;
+        // widgets (compass, lives, hints) take dx = +edge (the compass also
+        // takes the extra offset above). A wider screen (edge > 0) pushes
+        // both outward to the edges; a narrower screen (edge < 0) pulls both
+        // inward so they stay visible and at the edges. dy is always 0 and
+        // the scale is always 1: this patch only translates, never resizes.
+        tdx = base;
     }
     // A manual or automatic identity (16:9, no move, no resize, not hidden)
     // is nothing to do: skip the table entirely, so a no-op element never
